- content_for :title, "BaldrickDMX Tech Specs - Baldrick Board Documentation"

= render 'boards/shared/content_page', board_id: 'baldrickdmx', page_title: 'Technical Specifications', current_page: 'Tech Specs', page_subtitle: 'Board components and detailed specifications for BaldrickDMX', document_title: "BaldrickDMX Tech Specs - Baldrick Board Documentation" do
  .prose.max-w-none
    h2.text-3xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-6 Board Components

    .bg-white.rounded-lg.shadow-md.p-6.mb-6
      = image_tag "baldrickdmx/breakdown.png", class: "w-full rounded-lg mb-6", alt: "BaldrickDMX Board Overview"

      ol.list-decimal.list-inside.text-gray-700.space-y-3
        li
          strong QR Code - 
          | An easy to scan QR code which will take you to these docs for easy troubleshooting.
        li
          strong DMX OUTPUT RJ45 - 
          | With a helpful reminder 
          strong NOT TO PLUG THIS PORT ON YOUR NETWORK
          | .
        li
          strong DMX OUTPUT 3 PIN - 
          | A fancy schmancy Neutrik XLR.
        li
          strong DMX OUTPUT 5 PIN - 
          | A fancy schmancy Neutrik XLR.
        li
          strong Power input - 
          | You've got the choice of a Phoenix connector or barrel jack 
          strong (DO NOT USE BOTH)
          | , these can take 5v to 24v (or up to 48v on version 1.1) and will automatically step down to power the components, no jumpers needed.
        li
          strong Ethernet port - 
          | Plug this into your show network.
        li
          strong DMX Termination switch - 
          | DMX cables need to have their ends properly terminated to prevent any issues with the signal. Sometimes, the cable plugs have this built-in, but if they don't, this switch lets you do it right there. 
          br
          em.text-sm.text-gray-600 
            | (On some boards this switch may be hard to shift due to the coating process, a quick push with a flat head screwdriver should move it easily, we've learned from this and will be revising this button placement in the next revision.)
        li
          strong Button - 
          | The BaldrickDMX comes with a button on the board for factory reset functionality. 
          p.mt-1 This button is in case you break the board and need to reset it to factory settings. 
          p.mt-1 
            | When held for 5 seconds 
            strong during the board boot process
            | , the controller will reset to factory settings, everything will be removed including the latest firmware and it will be in the 'shipping state' where you click to update to the latest firmware.

      .bg-yellow-50.border-l-4.border-yellow-400.p-4.mb-6.mt-4
        .flex
          .flex-shrink-0
            svg.h-5.w-5.text-yellow-400 viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"
              path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.257 3.099c.765-1.36 2.722-1.36 3.486 0l5.58 9.92c.75 1.334-.213 2.98-1.742 2.98H4.42c-1.53 0-2.493-1.646-1.743-2.98l5.58-9.92zM11 13a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zm-1-8a1 1 0 00-1 1v3a1 1 0 002 0V6a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"
          .ml-3
            p.text-yellow-700.font-semibold
              strong Important: 
              | Mounting Holes - we've designed the BaldrickDMX to not only be as compact as possible, we've matched the mounting holes to other Baldrick boards so mounts can be reused. 
              strong DO NOT DRILL out 
              | these holes to make them fit the screws you've got already, doing this will void any warranty.
